      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2018-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>The equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x^3+x^2-1=0\"></span> has exactly one real root.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that, for this equation, the Newton-Raphson formula can be written<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\frac{4x_n^3+x_n^2+1}{6x_n^2+2x_n}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Using the formula given in part (a) with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_3\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Explain why, for this question, the Newton-Raphson method cannot be used with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=0\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
