      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=-3x^3+8x^2-9x+10,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Calculate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(2)\"></span></li><li>Write <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> as a product of two algebraic factors.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Using the answer to (a)(ii),</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>prove that there are exactly two real solutions to the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-3y^6+8y^4-9y^2+10=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>deduce the number of real solutions, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7\\pi\\leqslant\\theta&lt;10\\pi\"></span>, to the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3\\tan^3\\theta-8\\tan^2\\theta+9\\tan\\theta-10=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
