    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2018-june/q10",
      "question": "<p>A spherical mint of radius 5&#8239;mm is placed in the mouth and sucked.<br>Four minutes later, the radius of the mint is 3&#8239;mm.</p><p>In a simple model, the rate of decrease of the radius of the mint is inversely proportional to the square of the radius.</p><p>Using this model and all the information given,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find an equation linking the radius of the mint and the time.<br>(You should define the variables that you use.) <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence find the total time taken for the mint to completely dissolve. Give your answer in minutes and seconds to the nearest second. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Suggest a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
