      "question": "<p>A scientist is studying a population of mice on an island.</p><p>The number of mice, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span>, in the population, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> months after the start of the study, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N=\\frac{900}{3+7\\mathrm e^{-0.25t}},\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb R,\\quad t\\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the number of mice in the population at the start of the study. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Show that the rate of growth <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dN}{\\mathrm dt}\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dN}{\\mathrm dt}=\\dfrac{N(300-N)}{1200}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The rate of growth is a maximum after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> months.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find, according to the model, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>According to the model, the maximum number of mice on the island is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
